## Outcome

Fitmob was acquired by their direct competitor, ClassPass, in 2015. As a founding member of the team starting in 2013, I lead the startup from an idea to a user-friendly website, app, and in-person experience through design.

### Strategic

The design process was tightly integrated with senior leadership to allow rapid ideation and iteration of business needs while we found our way to product market fit. I worked directly with the team to translate service ventures into simple and digestible user flows within our digital products. From the start of the company, we introduced:

- Free, local fitness classes around San Francisco
- A paid subscription for first and third-party fitness classes
- Iterations on pricing models and messaging
- A parallel gym service to accompany fitness classes
- Small, dedicated fitness groups as a service
- Expansion of the service to other US cities
- - many other smaller iterations

### Tactical

I served roles in User Experience, Visual Design, and occasional front-end development. This often led to a design process that started focused on product design, transitioning into interactions, then production work through visual design and HTML/CSS.
